    "recommendations": "Addressing the single access point and extended driveway length could significantly improve emergency response effectiveness at this property. Ensuring the driveway remains clear of obstructions and wide enough to support two-way emergency vehicle movement would assist responders in both entry and egress during active operations. Where feasible, identifying or establishing a secondary access route to the rear of the property may enhance operational flexibility, particularly given the limited rear access observed. Maintaining visibility along the driveway corridor through the areas of dense vegetation could support faster navigation and improve situational awareness for arriving personnel. Clearly marked access points and designated staging areas near the main building and detached structure would further support coordinated emergency operations."
